From b8bd4cb07be40a88022e5eee2a5b6096778b0008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 07:48:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] meson/qtgui: forward CXXFLAGS/CFLAGS to qmake on macOS

librecoll.dylib is built by meson with the environment's CXXFLAGS (e.g.
MacPorts' -D_GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI=0 for the gcc/libstdc++ PPC build),
but qtgui/qmkmk.sh's qmake/make sub-build only had the compiler paths
forwarded, not the flags. qtgui object files therefore got compiled
against a different libstdc++ ABI than librecoll, and linking recoll
failed with undefined "...B5cxx11" symbols.

Also fix qmkmk.sh's use of unquoted $* when re-invoking qmake: it was
re-splitting arguments on whitespace, which would have shredded the
new multi-flag QMAKE_CXXFLAGS+=... argument into bogus separate qmake
arguments. Use "$@" to preserve argument boundaries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ETQGUDPX1v5NtrqGv5qPp8
---
 src/qtgui/meson.build | 13 +++++++++++++
 src/qtgui/qmkmk.sh    |  5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/qtgui/meson.build b/src/qtgui/meson.build
index 5fbaabf6..da37c366 100644
--- a/src/qtgui/meson.build
+++ b/src/qtgui/meson.build
@@ -69,6 +69,19 @@ if host_machine.system() == 'darwin'
         'QMAKE_LINK_C=' + cc_path,
         'QMAKE_LINK_C_SHLIB=' + cc_path,
     ]
+    # Same reasoning for compiler flags: CXXFLAGS/CFLAGS from the environment (e.g. MacPorts'
+    # -D_GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI=0, needed to match librecoll.dylib's ABI) end up in meson's
+    # cpp_args/c_args build options, but qmake's mkspec knows nothing about them. Without this,
+    # qtgui gets built against a different libstdc++ ABI than librecoll and fails to link with
+    # "undefined symbol ...B5cxx11" errors.
+    cpp_args = get_option('cpp_args')
+    if cpp_args.length() > 0
+        qmakevars += ['QMAKE_CXXFLAGS+=' + ' '.join(cpp_args)]
+    endif
+    c_args = get_option('c_args')
+    if c_args.length() > 0
+        qmakevars += ['QMAKE_CFLAGS+=' + ' '.join(c_args)]
+    endif
 endif
 recoll = custom_target(
     'recoll',
diff --git a/src/qtgui/qmkmk.sh b/src/qtgui/qmkmk.sh
index b76fa749..a59b4668 100755
--- a/src/qtgui/qmkmk.sh
+++ b/src/qtgui/qmkmk.sh
@@ -25,7 +25,10 @@ if test -z "$ncpus" ; then
 fi
 
 cd $dir
-${QMAKE} $fn $*
+# Use "$@" (not $*) so a qmake var assignment containing spaces (e.g. a multi-flag
+# QMAKE_CXXFLAGS+=... passed as one argument) reaches qmake intact instead of being
+# re-split on whitespace.
+"${QMAKE}" "$fn" "$@"
 ${MAKE} -j $ncpus
 
 if test `uname -s` = Darwin ; then
-- 
